<title>USA: 360 Communications sells $200 mln notes.</title>
<headline>360 Communications sells $200 mln notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from 360 Communications Co was priced on Wednesday, according to lead manager Salomon Brothers.</p>
<p>360 Communications is a cellular telephone company that also offers residental long distance and paging services.</p>
<p>BORROWER 360 COMMUNICATIONS CO</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	 COUPON 7.60 PCT   MATURITY 4/1/2009</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.838  FIRST PAY DATE 10/1/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BA1   YIELD 7.62 PCT    PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BBB-MINUS SPREAD 103 BPS    MAKE-WHOLE CALL AT 20</p>
<p>						 BASIS POINTS OVER U.S.</p>
<p>						     TREASURIES</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1678))</p>
</text>
